  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Current measured by the ammeter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced></math> in the reported circuit when no current flows through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance, will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0142_13b0fc6042de.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 187px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0142_13b0fc6042de.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 187px;\" /></p><p>This is a Wheatstone circuit. For the current to be zero in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> the Wheatstone circuit should be balanced. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Now, the equivalent resistance across the battery will be,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, the current measured by the ammeter is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
}